      "text": "Construction began on the Amsterdam Canal Ring, a series of concentric canals that are now a UNESCO World Heritage Site."
    },
    {
      "date": "1648",
      "headline": "Peace of Westphalia",
      "text": "The Peace of Westphalia ended the Eighty Years' War, recognizing the independence of the Dutch Republic and solidifying Amsterdam's position as a major trade center."
    },
    {
      "date": "1806",
      "headline": "Kingdom of Holland",
      "text": "Napoleon Bonaparte established the Kingdom of Holland, with Amsterdam as its capital."
    },
    {
      "date": "1813",
      "headline": "End of French Rule",
      "text": "The French were expelled from the Netherlands, and Amsterdam became part of the newly established Kingdom of the Netherlands."
    },
    {
      "date": "1940-1945",
      "headline": "World War II Occupation",
      "text": "Amsterdam was occupied by Nazi Germany during World War II, leading to significant hardship and the deportation of many Jewish residents."
    },
    {
      "date": "1975",
      "headline": "Amsterdam Metro Opens",
      "text": "The first line of the Amsterdam Metro was opened, improving public transportation in the city."
    },
    {
      "date": "2010",
      "headline": "Canal Ring Becomes UNESCO Site",
