      "headline": "Adolf Hitler Becomes Leader",
      "text": "Adolf Hitler was appointed as the leader of the Nazi Party, gaining dictatorial powers within the party."
    },
    {
      "date": "1923-11-08",
      "headline": "Beer Hall Putsch",
      "text": "The Nazi Party attempted a coup in Munich, known as the Beer Hall Putsch, which failed and resulted in the arrest of Adolf Hitler and other leaders."
    },
    {
      "date": "1925-02-27",
      "headline": "Re-founding of the Nazi Party",
      "text": "After being banned following the Beer Hall Putsch, the Nazi Party was re-founded with a focus on legal means to gain power."
    },
    {
      "date": "1930",
      "headline": "Rise in Popularity",
      "text": "The Nazi Party gained significant support during the Great Depression, becoming the second-largest party in the Reichstag after the 1930 elections."
    },
