      "headline": "Hitler Appointed Chancellor",
      "text": "Adolf Hitler was appointed Chancellor of Germany, marking the beginning of Nazi control over the German government."
    },
    {
      "date": "1933-03-23",
      "headline": "Enabling Act Passed",
      "text": "The Reichstag passed the Enabling Act, which gave Hitler's government dictatorial powers and effectively ended democratic governance in Germany."
    },
    {
      "date": "1934-06-30",
      "headline": "Night of the Long Knives",
      "text": "A purge within the Nazi Party, known as the Night of the Long Knives, saw the elimination of potential rivals and consolidation of Hitler's power."
    },
    {
      "date": "1935-09-15",
      "headline": "Nuremberg Laws Enacted",
      "text": "The Nuremberg Laws were enacted, institutionalizing racial discrimination against Jews and laying the groundwork for future anti-Semitic policies."
    },
    {
      "date": "1939-09-01",
      "headline": "Invasion of Poland",
      "text": "Germany invaded Poland, leading to the outbreak of World War II."
    },
    {
      "date": "1945-05-08",
      "headline": "End of World War II and Nazi Party",
