      "date": "-0423",
      "headline": "Mention in Aristophanes' Play 'The Clouds'",
      "text": "Socrates was satirized in Aristophanes' play 'The Clouds,' which was first performed in 423 BCE. The play portrays Socrates as a sophist and mocks his philosophical ideas."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0407",
      "headline": "Association with Alcibiades",
      "text": "Socrates was known to have a close relationship with Alcibiades, a prominent Athenian statesman and general. Their association was controversial due to Alcibiades' political actions and eventual defection to Sparta."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0399",
      "headline": "Trial and Death of Socrates",
      "text": "In 399 BCE, Socrates was put on trial for impiety and corrupting the youth of Athens. He was found guilty and sentenced to death by drinking a cup of poison hemlock. Socrates spent his last day in prison, where he discussed philosophical topics with his followers before his execution."
    }
  ]
}

