      "headline": "Sarsen Stones Added",
      "text": "By 2500 BCE, the large sarsen stones were added to Stonehenge, forming the iconic outer circle and central trilithons."
    },
    {
      "date": "-02400",
      "headline": "Rearrangement of Bluestones",
      "text": "Around 2400 BCE, the bluestones were rearranged into the horseshoe and circle that are visible today."
    },
    {
      "date": "-02200",
      "headline": "Final Construction Phase",
      "text": "The final known construction phase occurred around 2200 BCE, with further rearrangement of the bluestones and the addition of the Altar Stone."
    },
    {
      "date": "-01600",
      "headline": "End of Major Construction",
      "text": "By 1600 BCE, major construction at Stonehenge had ceased, although the site continued to be used for ceremonial purposes."
    },
