      "text": "Medusa, one of the three Gorgon sisters, is born to the primordial sea deities Phorcys and Ceto. Unlike her sisters, Euryale and Stheno, Medusa is mortal."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0600",
      "headline": "Transformation into a Gorgon",
      "text": "Medusa is transformed into a Gorgon by the goddess Athena. According to myth, this transformation was a punishment for desecrating Athena's temple."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0500",
      "headline": "Medusa's Appearance",
      "text": "Medusa is described as having snakes for hair and a gaze that turns anyone who looks at her into stone. Her monstrous appearance becomes a symbol of fear and power."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0490",
      "headline": "Death of Medusa",
      "text": "Medusa is slain by the hero Perseus. Using a mirrored shield given to him by Athena, Perseus avoids Medusa's petrifying gaze and beheads her while she sleeps."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0489",
      "headline": "Birth of Pegasus and Chrysaor",
      "text": "From Medusa's blood, the winged horse Pegasus and the giant Chrysaor are born. These offspring emerge as Perseus carries Medusa's head away."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0488",
      "headline": "Medusa's Head as a Weapon",
      "text": "Perseus uses Medusa's head as a weapon to petrify his enemies, including the sea monster Cetus, to save Andromeda, and later to turn King Polydectes to stone."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0487",
      "headline": "Medusa's Head on Athena's Shield",
      "text": "Athena places Medusa's head on her shield, the Aegis, as a protective symbol. The Gorgoneion becomes a powerful emblem in Greek art and mythology."
    }
  ]
}

