      "text": "Wilhelm II began a significant expansion of the German Navy in 1897, aiming to challenge British naval supremacy, which contributed to rising tensions leading up to World War I."
    },
    {
      "date": "1914-07-28",
      "headline": "World War I Begins",
      "text": "World War I began on July 28, 1914, with Germany, under Wilhelm II's rule, playing a central role in the conflict as part of the Central Powers."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918-11-09",
      "headline": "Abdication of Wilhelm II",
      "text": "Wilhelm II abdicated the throne on November 9, 1918, as Germany faced defeat in World War I and revolution at home, leading to the end of the German Empire."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918-11-10",
      "headline": "Exile in the Netherlands",
      "text": "Following his abdication, Wilhelm II fled to the Netherlands on November 10, 1918, where he lived in exile for the rest of his life."
    },
    {
