      "text": "Trotsky moved to Nikolayev to attend school, where he became involved in revolutionary activities."
    },
    {
      "date": "1898",
      "headline": "Arrest and Exile to Siberia",
      "text": "Trotsky was arrested for revolutionary activities and exiled to Siberia."
    },
    {
      "date": "1902",
      "headline": "Escape from Siberia",
      "text": "Trotsky escaped from Siberia, adopting the pseudonym 'Trotsky' and moving to London to join the Russian Social Democratic Labour Party."
    },
    {
      "date": "1905",
      "headline": "Role in the 1905 Revolution",
      "text": "Trotsky became a key figure in the 1905 Russian Revolution, serving as chairman of the St. Petersburg Soviet."
    },
    {
      "date": "1906",
      "headline": "Arrest and Second Exile",
      "text": "Following the failure of the 1905 Revolution, Trotsky was arrested and exiled again to Siberia."
    },
    {
      "date": "1907",
      "headline": "Escape and European Exile",
      "text": "Trotsky escaped from Siberia once more and spent the next decade in various European countries, continuing his revolutionary activities."
    },
    {
      "date": "1917-03",
      "headline": "Return to Russia",
      "text": "Trotsky returned to Russia after the February Revolution, joining the Bolshevik Party."
    },
    {
      "date": "1917-11",
      "headline": "October Revolution",
      "text": "Trotsky played a leading role in the Bolshevik seizure of power during the October Revolution, serving as the People's Commissar for Foreign Affairs."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918",
      "headline": "Role in Treaty of Brest-Litovsk",
      "text": "Trotsky led the Soviet delegation in negotiations with Germany, resulting in the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk."
    },
    {
      "date": "1918-1920",
      "headline": "Leadership in the Russian Civil War",
      "text": "As People's Commissar of Military and Naval Affairs, Trotsky organized and led the Red Army to victory in the Russian Civil War."
    },
    {
      "date": "1923",
      "headline": "Decline in Power",
      "text": "Trotsky's influence began to wane as Joseph Stalin consolidated power within the Communist Party."
    },
    {
      "date": "1927",
      "headline": "Expulsion from the Communist Party",
      "text": "Trotsky was expelled from the Communist Party due to his opposition to Stalin's policies."
    },
    {
      "date": "1929",
      "headline": "Exile from the Soviet Union",
      "text": "Trotsky was deported from the Soviet Union and began his life in exile, living in various countries."
    },
    {
      "date": "1938",
      "headline": "Founding of the Fourth International",
      "text": "Trotsky founded the Fourth International, an organization of communist parties opposed to Stalinism."
    },
    {
      "date": "1940-08-21",
      "headline": "Assassination",
      "text": "Trotsky was assassinated in Mexico City by Ramón Mercader, an agent of the Soviet NKVD."
