      "headline": "Elected President",
      "text": "John Quincy Adams was elected as the sixth President of the United States after a contentious election decided by the House of Representatives."
    },
    {
      "date": "1829",
      "headline": "End of Presidency",
      "text": "Adams's term as President ended, and he was succeeded by Andrew Jackson."
    },
    {
      "date": "1830",
      "headline": "Elected to the House of Representatives",
      "text": "Adams was elected to the U.S. House of Representatives, where he served for 17 years, becoming a leading opponent of slavery."
    },
    {
      "date": "1841",
      "headline": "Amistad Case",
      "text": "Adams successfully argued before the Supreme Court for the freedom of African captives in the Amistad case."
    },
    {
