      "headline": "British Conquest",
      "text": "Montreal was captured by British forces during the Seven Years' War, marking the end of French rule in the city. This event was part of the larger British conquest of New France."
    },
    {
      "date": "1832",
      "headline": "Incorporation as a City",
      "text": "Montreal was incorporated as a city in 1832, allowing for a structured municipal government and the ability to manage local affairs more effectively."
    },
    {
      "date": "1849",
      "headline": "Burning of the Parliament Buildings",
      "text": "The Parliament Buildings in Montreal were burned down by a mob in 1849, an event that led to the relocation of the capital of the Province of Canada from Montreal to Toronto."
    },
    {
      "date": "1967",
      "headline": "Expo 67",
      "text": "Montreal hosted the World's Fair, known as Expo 67, which was one of the most successful international exhibitions of the 20th century. It celebrated Canada's centennial and showcased the city on the global stage."
    },
    {
      "date": "1976",
      "headline": "1976 Summer Olympics",
      "text": "Montreal hosted the 1976 Summer Olympics, becoming the first Canadian city to host the Olympic Games. The event was marked by the construction of the iconic Olympic Stadium."
    },
    {
      "date": "1995",
      "headline": "Quebec Referendum",
