      "text": "eBay was founded by Pierre Omidyar in September 1995. Originally called AuctionWeb, it was created as a site for people to list and bid on items in an auction format."
    },
    {
      "date": "1997-09",
      "headline": "Company Name Changed to eBay",
      "text": "In September 1997, AuctionWeb officially changed its name to eBay. The name was derived from Echo Bay Technology Group, Omidyar's consulting firm."
    },
    {
      "date": "1998-09-21",
      "headline": "eBay Goes Public",
      "text": "eBay went public on September 21, 1998, with its initial public offering (IPO) on the NASDAQ stock exchange under the ticker symbol EBAY."
    },
    {
      "date": "2002-10",
      "headline": "Acquisition of PayPal",
      "text": "In October 2002, eBay acquired PayPal, an online payment company, for $1.5 billion in stock. This acquisition helped streamline transactions on the eBay platform."
    },
    {
      "date": "2005-08",
      "headline": "Acquisition of Skype",
      "text": "eBay acquired Skype, a voice-over-IP service, in August 2005 for approximately $2.6 billion. The acquisition aimed to enhance communication between buyers and sellers."
    },
    {
      "date": "2008-09",
      "headline": "Launch of eBay Classifieds",
      "text": "In September 2008, eBay launched eBay Classifieds, a platform for local classified advertisements, expanding its reach in the online marketplace."
    },
    {
      "date": "2015-07-17",
      "headline": "Spin-off of PayPal",
      "text": "On July 17, 2015, eBay completed the spin-off of PayPal into a separate publicly traded company, allowing both companies to focus on their core businesses."
    },
    {
      "date": "2020-07",
      "headline": "Sale of Classifieds Business",
      "text": "In July 2020, eBay announced the sale of its Classifieds business to Adevinta for $9.2 billion, focusing more on its core marketplace business."
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-06",
      "headline": "Sale of eBay Korea",
      "text": "In June 2021, eBay agreed to sell its South Korean business to Emart for $3 billion, as part of its strategy to streamline operations."
    },
    {
      "date": "2023",
      "headline": "eBay's Global Reach in 2023",
      "text": "By 2023, eBay had 132 million yearly active buyers worldwide and handled $73 billion in transactions, with 48% occurring in the United States. The company had a take rate of 13.81%."
    }
  ]
}

