      "text": "The Hmong people are believed to have settled in the Yellow River region of China around 3000 BCE, according to some historical and anthropological studies."
    },
    {
      "date": "1600",
      "headline": "Migration to Southeast Asia",
      "text": "Due to pressures from Chinese expansion and conflicts, many Hmong began migrating southward into Southeast Asia, including areas that are now Vietnam, Laos, and Thailand."
