      "headline": "Construction of Angkor Wat",
      "text": "Angkor Wat was constructed as a Hindu temple dedicated to the deity Vishnu. It was built by the Khmer King Suryavarman II in the early 12th century in Yasodharapura, the capital of the Khmer Empire."
    },
    {
      "date": "1177",
      "headline": "Sack of Angkor",
      "text": "The city of Angkor was sacked by the Chams, traditional enemies of the Khmer, which led to a period of decline for the Khmer Empire."
    },
    {
      "date": "1181",
      "headline": "Jayavarman VII's Reign",
      "text": "Jayavarman VII ascended to the throne and began a series of construction projects, including the transformation of Angkor Wat into a Buddhist temple."
    },
    {
      "date": "1296",
      "headline": "Visit by Zhou Daguan",
      "text": "The Chinese diplomat Zhou Daguan visited Angkor and provided one of the most detailed accounts of the Khmer Empire and Angkor Wat during its peak."
    },
    {
      "date": "1431",
      "headline": "Fall of Angkor",
      "text": "Angkor was abandoned after a series of invasions by the Ayutthaya Kingdom, marking the end of the Khmer Empire's dominance in the region."
    },
    {
      "date": "1860",
      "headline": "Rediscovery by Henri Mouhot",
      "text": "French explorer Henri Mouhot popularized Angkor Wat in the West after his travels to Cambodia, leading to increased interest and study of the site."
    },
    {
      "date": "1992",
      "headline": "UNESCO World Heritage Site",
      "text": "Angkor Wat was designated as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, recognizing its cultural and historical significance."
    }
  ]
}

